  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: model forecasts are systematically too high versus realized prices, especially during downtrends. Apply a downward level shift to the entire path (largest in the first ~1–2 weeks).",
    "Trend/turning-point lag: after a peak, the model is slow to recognize regime change and keeps projecting sideways-to-higher prices while outcomes fall. Add a rule that increases negative drift when recent returns turn negative or when price breaks below short-term moving averages.",
    "Overshoot on rebounds/spikes: the model tends to extrapolate short-lived upticks into multi-week strength, but realized prices mean-revert lower. Damp forecast responses to 1–3 day rallies (cap the impact of recent positive returns).",
    "Insufficient mean reversion: forecasts remain anchored near recent highs (upper 70s/80s) while outcomes revert toward a lower band (~68–73). Increase pull toward a rolling medium-term mean/median, with stronger reversion at longer horizons (weeks 3–4).",
    "Horizon-specific error shape: errors grow with horizon; weeks 3–4 often drift upward in the forecast while realized prices stay flat-to-lower. Impose a non-positive drift constraint beyond ~10–15 days unless there is sustained multi-day momentum."
  ]
}
